@* ---------- FAQ ---------- *@
<section class="faq" id="faq">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="section-head">
            <div class="eyebrow dark">
                <MudIcon Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.HelpOutline" Style="font-size:16px;" />
                <span>Frequently asked</span>
            </div>
            <h2>Answers before you sign up.</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-grid">
            <details class="faq-item">
                <summary>Is there really a free plan, forever?</summary>
                <p>Yes. The Homestead plan is free for up to 10 goats and never expires. No credit card required to start.</p>
            </details>
            <details class="faq-item">
                <summary>Can buyers actually find my farm on GoatLab?</summary>
                <p>
                    Yes — that's the marketplace half of the product. When you flip on your public farm
                    page and mark goats "for sale," they show up in the breed directory at
                    <MudLink Href="/breeds" Underline="Underline.Always">/breeds</MudLink>, are indexed
                    by Google with rich-result structured data, and can be filtered by sex, price, and
                    state. Buyers can follow your farm to be notified the next time you list.
                </p>
            </details>
            <details class="faq-item">
                <summary>What's "cross-farm lineage"?</summary>
                <p>
                    Every public goat gets a lineage page that walks pedigree four generations deep. If
                    one of the ancestors is on another GoatLab farm (matched by registration number),
                    that ancestor becomes a clickable link to its own lineage. A buyer can verify that
                    the sire really is at Cedar Farm and was bred by Mountain Farm — no email tag,
                    no scanned PDFs. The closest thing the goat world has to a Carfax.
                </p>
            </details>
            <details class="faq-item">
                <summary>Can I sell goats through GoatLab?</summary>
                <p>
                    Yes. List a goat for sale, set an asking price, and (optionally) a deposit
                    percentage. Buyers can reserve via Stripe Checkout — the deposit goes straight to
                    your waitlist, the customer record is created automatically, and the funds land in
                    your Stripe balance. When the sale completes you can transfer the goat to the buyer
                    if they're also on GoatLab — all the records move with it.
                </p>
            </details>
            <details class="faq-item">
                <summary>Can my vet see records without signing up?</summary>
                <p>
                    Yes. From any goat's detail page, click <strong>Share with vet</strong> — GoatLab
                    mints a one-time URL with a configurable expiry. The vet opens it on their phone:
                    no app install, no account. They see medical history, weights, FAMACHA, body
                    condition. They can leave a note that lands on the goat's timeline as a Checkup
                    record. Revoke the link anytime.
                </p>
            </details>
            <details class="faq-item">
                <summary>Does GoatLab work offline in the barn?</summary>
                <p>Yes. Install GoatLab as a PWA on your phone or tablet and it keeps working with no signal. Your logs sync automatically the next time you're online.</p>
            </details>
            <details class="faq-item">
                <summary>Can I self-host GoatLab on my own server?</summary>
                <p>
                    Absolutely — GoatLab is open source and ships as a Docker image. Grab the repo from
                    <MudLink Href="@RepoUrl" Target="_blank" Underline="Underline.Always">@RepoUrl</MudLink>
                    and follow the self-hosting guide. Everything in the hosted version is in the container.
                </p>
            </details>
            <details class="faq-item">
                <summary>Where is my data stored?</summary>
                <p>On the hosted service, your data lives in an encrypted database in our cloud. If you self-host, it lives wherever your Docker volumes live — your NAS, your Pi, your server. You can export to CSV any time.</p>
            </details>
            <details class="faq-item">
                <summary>What devices does it run on?</summary>
                <p>Any modern browser — iPhone, Android, iPad, Windows, Mac, Linux. The dashboard is responsive and touch-friendly, with an installable PWA for offline use.</p>
            </details>
            <details class="faq-item">
                <summary>Can I import my existing spreadsheet?</summary>
                <p>Yes. Import your herd from CSV on day one. Milk records, kidding history, and sales can also be bulk-imported.</p>
            </details>
            <details class="faq-item">
                <summary>What if I want to cancel or switch to self-hosting later?</summary>
                <p>No lock-in. Export your full farm to CSV, spin up the Docker container, and import. You own your data.</p>
            </details>
            <details class="faq-item">
                <summary>Who's behind GoatLab?</summary>
                <p>Goat people who got tired of managing herds in a notebook. We build in the open on GitHub — issues, roadmap, and contributions welcome at <MudLink Href="@RepoUrl" Target="_blank" Underline="Underline.Always">@RepoUrl</MudLink>.</p>
            </details>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

